  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "I fixed `add_tag` in `tag_util.py`, and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes (1 test).\n\n**The bug:** `add_tag(record, tag, tags=[])` used an empty list as its default. Python creates that list once and reuses it, so every call that left out `tags` added to the same list, and tags from one record showed up on another.\n\n**The fix:** the default is now `tags=None`, and the function creates a new empty list when `tags` isn't passed. If the caller passes their own list, it's used as given, as the README asks. `remove_tag` is unchanged.\n\nDONE: Fixed add_tag's mutable default argument (tags=[] \u2192 tags=None with a new list per call); public test passes.",
