      "final_message": "I rewrote `semver_compare` in `solution.py` so it follows the README, and both public tests pass.\n\n- **Validation:** each input must be exactly `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, and each part must be `0` or an ASCII number with no leading zero. The whole string has to match, so a trailing newline doesn't slip through. A non-string argument raises `TypeError`; any other invalid string raises `ValueError`.\n- **Comparison:** the two versions are compared as number tuples, returning -1, 0 or 1.\n\nBeyond the two public tests, I checked a few cases by hand:\n- `1.10.0` counts as greater than `1.9.9`.\n- `2.0.0` counts as less than `10.0.0`.\n- Two-part versions, `-a` suffixes, leading zeros, leading spaces, non-ASCII digits, a trailing newline and empty strings are all rejected.\n- A non-string argument raises `TypeError`.\n\nDONE: Repaired semver_compare to strictly validate MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH (no leading zeros, TypeError/ValueError) and compare as (major, minor, patch) tuples returning -1/0/1; public tests pass.",
